commit 7816c335faded133c8138eb6fbfe3ed8c009d17d
Author: squidllee <crmonk127@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 06:46:53 2026 -0400

    perf(library): read only card fields for card queries

    Card reads loaded each row's full ocr_text and metadata — including
    article html, text, and extractedText — and cardItem discarded nearly
    all of it on the main-process event loop. A card-only projection now
    trims and truncates ocr_text in SQL (JS-trim semantics via an explicit
    character set), keeps only the metadata keys a card reads behind a
    json_valid guard so one malformed row degrades instead of failing the
    list, and reduces '$.html' to a marker so hasArticleContent is
    unchanged. detailColumns/getItem are untouched; cardItem drops its
    now-redundant re-trim, which would have stripped boundary whitespace
    the slice must keep.

    SWE-2 High via T3 Code.

    Generated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)

    Co-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

